A||||7||Chance||Possible clutch/shifting solution||||14||
Z||000000||Chance||10-10-2000||05:18 AM||||For quite a few months, I had my fiero parked due to the fact that It was nearly impossible to shift, and the local shop where I got the clutch replaced a little over a year ago told me "Needs a new clutch" AGAIN (and I drive like an old man to boot) and Im not paying them the 950 buck they want THIS time... I replaced the slave and bled it... nothing, the Master was replaced when a new clutch was put in, so I didn't mess with that... the whole thing disgusted me because SOMETIMES, I could get in, start it, and it would shift like nothing was wrong. then turn it off, or go along, and it wouldn't shift unless I shut the engine off.  Well, I guess I was desprate because the motor in my pathfider blew up, so I needed my car. Messing around, I tried everything I could, I drove it back home from my partents where it was parked, (shuting it off to get to first and all) when I looked at the tran...I have an 86GT 5 speed and it has a dip stick... I checked it, and thought the oil was kind of thick, so I sucked out about a quart, and put in a qt of mobile 5-30 Synthetic...I rememberd also before all this happed, I think I added SOME oil when I first got it, but I decided to remove more then a qt, and just add the qt of Syn5-30... belive it or not, Its not 100 back to normal, but its SHIFTING 90 percent of the time now... so I would check that out||||reg||14
Z||000001||862M4inCA||10-10-2000||05:35 AM||||Just a thought, does it look like someone had previously used 85-90W or thicker in it? Also, isn't it recommended that the oil be changed occasionally? It's possible that when you added the new oil, that it thinned the "sludge" that was in it enough to allow smoother shifting.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Chance||10-10-2000||06:06 AM||||The shop where I took it a while back COULD of put some in there, also, I was wondering, since tomorrow, Im going to drain it totally, and refill with new,  what should I use? some reference I have seen use dexron/atf fluid, or should i stick with the 5-30????||||reg||1
Z||000003||862M4inCA||10-11-2000||04:43 AM||||Well, if I were you, I would stick with the manufacturers recommendation and stick with the 5-30. They tend to know more about their "creations" than anyone else. ||||reg||1
