Z||000005||862M4inCA||10-11-2000||05:02 PM||||they all have a "dipstick" of some sort. I know on mine, and likely most everyone with a standard, you pull the VSS out, and there are two marks on the VSS. these are the "lo" and "hi" marks for the fluid level.||||reg||1
Z||000006||lowCG||10-11-2000||08:39 PM||||The closest I've come to perfection is by using the "GM Syncromesh Fluid",costs $10 a quart,at the dealer,but is worth it I believe.<BR>BTW,thanks to whoever suggested this before, a couple months ago.||||reg||1
